;; A three-tile gap (columns 10-12) with the deep drop two rows down; the
;; east bank stands a tile higher. Eastward is the gust's crossing: from a
;; run in calm it barely carries, with the eastward gust over the gap it is
;; easy. Westward the drop to the lower bank carries in calm. Both banks are
;; out of the wind. (David's playtest, 2026-10-11: time the gust, not the
;; footwork; tools/cloudstair-takeoff.sgl measures the take-off windows.)
(room
  region: cloudstair
  at: (11 0)
  title: "Cloud Gap"
  intent: "a clear break in the ledge asks for a held drift as eastward gusts pass over slow cloud"
  bed: (wind 0.9 water 0.15 air 0.5 drone 0.3)
  light: 1
  sun: 1
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "#####              ######"
   "##                    ###"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "                         "
   "                 |  |    "
   "   |  | |    #########   "
   "##########   ############"
   "##########   ############"
   "##########xxx############")
  things: ((air-field at: (10 1) size: (3 8) kind: east-gust))
  decor: auto)
